[b]JMA Cluster Entries with Market Structure[/b] combines a 10-JMA cluster scoring system with full market structure context — Wyckoff phases and SMC Order Blocks — and marks trend entries on the JMA cluster flip.

[b]What it does[/b]

The core idea: JMA cluster alignment (how many of the 10 JMAs are stacked in the same direction) measures how broadly the trend has turned. An entry fires when the cluster flips, filtered by slope, by how many JMAs crossed on the bar, by the distance to the slow JMA, and by a cooldown. Wyckoff and order-block structure are drawn alongside as context.

[b]Signal components[/b]

[list]
[*][b]JMA cluster score[/b] — 0–100 alignment score across 10 Jurik Moving Averages
[*][b]Cluster flip trigger[/b] — entry when the cluster score crosses the threshold, with slope, score-jump and ATR-distance filters
[*][b]Market structure[/b] — Wyckoff phase/event detection and SMC Order Block system (BOS, displacement, scoring, mitigation tracking)
[/list]

[b]Timeframe presets[/b]

Lookbacks and parameters are automatically optimized for 15M, 1H, 4H, Daily, and Weekly charts. A dual-pivot system provides both live-ready and confirmed entry variants.

[b]Alerts[/b]
All alerts fire only on confirmed bar close by default (configurable via "Alerts only on bar close" toggle).
[list]
[*][b]Entry Long[/b] — bullish JMA cluster flip entry
[*][b]Entry Short[/b] — bearish JMA cluster flip entry
[/list]

